\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The counting product leaves the limit open}
\date{2026-11-15}

\p{The cubical torus of \ref{fdip-00OK}, with the counting
pairing, is not a smooth triangulation. Its pairing is not
the Whitney inner product of
\citet{Definition 4.1, p. 93}{dodziuk1976hodge}.
The eigenvalue bound and the #{\mathrm L^2} convergence of
Hodge summands in the [Whitney forms](fdip-00S2) are not
claimed for this counting product. That convergence is open.}

\p{The scaling in \ref{fdip-00S5} is an identity of finite
pairings. It does not supply the missing limit.}
